# Boards parity (BoardsController). Boards are not flag-gated, so the shared
# no-flags Vapor serves them. Reset the fixtures first, every run:
#   docker exec -i norviq-v2-schema-pg psql -U pg -d norviq < parity/boards-setup.sql
#   go run ./cmd/parity -a http://127.0.0.1:8081 -b http://127.0.0.1:18143 -jwt-secret parity-secret \
#     -cases parity/boards.jsonl -ignore requestId,id,createdAt
# (id/createdAt are only volatile on the create-post and create-comment
# cases; every read case also passes without that ignore, see the report.)
# Reads come first; the writes after them are idempotent or error paths, so
# Vapor (first) and v2 (second) see the same state. Order-dependent writes
# (create board, vote, delete) are in parity/boards-ordered.jsonl.
# Users: alice ...001, bob ...002, fresh ...003 (no guidelines), nouser
# ...004, muted ...005, banned ...006, suspended ...007, carol ...008.
